    {
      "id": "claim_f4a17d5b7ea74789acdae942490d00d2",
      "statement": "Since v0.4.0 every proxied cell call rides a pooled per-peer tunnel: HMAC-signed h1 upgrade establishment, then opaque plain HTTP that the hop never interprets, with a different protocol version refused at establishment, which makes the v0.3 to v0.4 upgrade stop-all.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main/peer_tunnel.rs#L3-L23",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:26269f01546823c869820dc920266cf3189fda11085cf7065f2f16ef02970096:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/README.md#L537-L544",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7876f607107540b4e896ea1525260282c4fda5db6b9e1ea616d74da502618f9d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_33b15e7efc654282877c2cf008c35e79",
      "statement": "Per-call control rides x-cells-* inner headers that the entry node overwrites and the exit node strips, so an application cannot smuggle reserved names in either direction; tunnels are plain h1 keep-alive pooled per peer because un-pooled calls exhausted the ephemeral port range near 1k calls/s.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main/peer_tunnel.rs#L14-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a4bad8ac2b372d5ec13b1ac86febb561891a6521c31fe3f1fa054f0700878b0c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_417985f1745b4279b31bab6fef70d42a",
      "statement": "Tunnel inner calls are not signed (bodies stream to the owner, so per-call HMAC is impossible); only establishment is authenticated, every path to a runtime class demands the fleet secret, and the signature provides neither confidentiality nor post-establishment authentication, leaving the private network as the trust boundary.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L60-L76",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:00cf77017aea99f2b9c5b2b77d075cda8636cd5bfe11e60d81c908332e3eb070:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2fb3bbcf32554f85a4603548fa917a39",
      "statement": "Peer authentication is HMAC-SHA256 over a canonical string binding domain, protocol version, method, path+query, body SHA-256, source, target, timestamp, and nonce, with a 30 s two-sided clock window, replay-cache retention pinned at compile time to at least twice the window, and protocol version 5 exchanged on x-cells-peer-version.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/peer_auth.rs#L17-L29",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:49533b1d08d38953b7d5dfbfe1fe71afe40d46d4cba1f21d7a8668aac0f8948f:"
